max mayfield is at the very center of  stranger things season four from her  iconic episode four scene to the  explosive finale here's everything you  need to know about that final  confrontation and what it might mean for  season five since the beginning stranger  things has kept a consistent record of  turning things up to 11 for its drama  and compelling emotional beats in  between decimating whatever dares to  step out from the upside down season 4  volume 1 of netflix's award-winning  series accomplished that before a  five-week break that felt like a year on  its own from there though alarms were  raised thanks to threats from the duffer  brothers promising a mad symphony of  chaos for volume two  i  think we're mad fools a lot of us it  turns out they weren't kidding the  mind-flare-sized double-dose of final  episodes hit us with plenty of emotional  gut punches with one devastating wallop  involving fan favorite max mayfield it's  fair to say that for most of this season  sadie sings performance as max has been  at the core of some of its most  heart-wrenching scenes besides putting  kate bush back on the charts it elevated  the character into one of the show's  biggest draws  now when i lie in bed at night  i  pray that something will happen to me  the hope was that she would help save  the day and be rewarded for her troubles  instead volume 2 ended in a bittersweet  victory against vecna in what was easily  one of the show's most powerful scenes  to date seeing any of the stranger  things characters hurt like this would  be a lot to take in but max's condition  at the end of episode 9 is especially  heartbreaking simply due to the time  spent getting to know her this season  between 11 trekking through max's  memories and max finally being honest  about her feelings regarding her  brother's death these emotional beats  allowed us to really connect with her  and see that she had a clear path ahead  that is until the duffer brothers pulled  the rug out from under us and got max  right where vekna wanted max's plan to  use herself as bait quickly turned south  despite eleven piggybacking her way in  to defend her although eleven was only  briefly out of the fight it was long  enough for max to endure a similar fate  as vechna's previous victims making for  an excruciating watch lucas looking on  helplessly as an invisible force snaps  his former flame's limbs was horrifying  but it also played a small part in  rectifying a significant issue in volume  1. after watching him question his  alliances in volume 1 seeing him battle  his former team captain jason and  accepting being outside the norm felt  long overdue this also allows him to be  at max's side during her darkest hour  setting up caleb mclaughlin to flex his  acting muscles and provide some of the  best work we've ever seen from him  culminating in one of the most visually  stunning moments not just of this season  but of the entire series lucas pleading  for max to come back would have turned  on the waterworks regardless but having  both of them be joined by 11 in her  barren and empty realm which we've seen  so many times before amplifies just how  huge the loss is watching max's friends  cry for her together while still apart  is a beautifully bleak sight one that is  revisited when eleven visits max in the  hospital it's like what papa said about  vekma's tactics he takes everything from  his victims everything they are and  everything they ever will be  their memories their abilities the  evidence of this is clear when eleven  makes one last attempt to psychically  link to max but finds nothing vekna  certainly went by the book but it's the  one we see lucas reading we should focus  on before her friends walk into max's  hospital room lucas is reading stephen  king and peter straub's 1984 book the  talisman a dark fantasy novel about a  boy who uses the titular item in an  attempt to save his mother from cancer  the talisman later adapted into a comic  book series takes place in a world of  alternate dimensions inhabited by  parallel individuals or twinners to  those living in ours these twinners can  possess their other selves and jump  between worlds but should one of them  die their doppelganger becomes single  natured this allows them to jump between  realities without needing a duplicate to  inhabit with this page turner in mind  could this hint at what's in store next  season how is vecna still alive after  being shot several times and all burned  up and where is he now might he still  have what remains of max as dr brennan  suggested could max be lost in another  reality herself beyond the upside down  if so a rematch and the fate of the  world could be in the cards for the  final season of stranger things our only  hope is that it can top the most metal  moment in history that was eddie's  rooftop guitar solo better get  practicing 11. check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about stranger things  season 4 are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one
 

